// ═══ THE TRAP — orElse ALWAYS evaluates! ═══

// CHEAP default — no difference:
String name = Optional.of("Rajesh").orElse("Unknown");          // "Unknown" computed but unused — trivial cost
String name = Optional.of("Rajesh").orElseGet(() -> "Unknown"); // "Unknown" NOT computed — but same trivial cost

// EXPENSIVE default — BIG difference:
Account account = Optional.of(cachedAccount)
    .orElse(accountRepo.findById("SAV2001").orElseThrow());
// (Caution) accountRepo.findById() EXECUTES even though cachedAccount is present!
// Unnecessary DB query! Wasted connection, wasted time.

Account account = Optional.of(cachedAccount)
    .orElseGet(() -> accountRepo.findById("SAV2001").orElseThrow());
// (Recommended) accountRepo.findById() NOT executed — Supplier lambda never called!
// DB query skipped. Zero waste.
```

**Proof with side effects:**

```java
private Account createDefaultAccount() {
    log.info(" Creating default account — EXPENSIVE OPERATION!");
    // Simulates: DB call, HTTP call, heavy computation
    return new Account("DEFAULT", BigDecimal.ZERO);
}

// orElse — createDefaultAccount() CALLED even when present:
Account result = Optional.of(existingAccount)
    .orElse(createDefaultAccount());
// Console: " Creating default account — EXPENSIVE OPERATION!"
// The method ran! But its result was thrown away because Optional was present.

// orElseGet — createDefaultAccount() NOT called when present:
Account result = Optional.of(existingAccount)
    .orElseGet(this::createDefaultAccount);
// Console: (nothing!) — Supplier never invoked.
```

**orElseThrow — the third option (fail fast):**

```java
Account account = findAccount("SAV2001")
    .orElseThrow(() -> new AccountNotFoundException("SAV2001"));
// Empty → throws exception. Present → returns value.
// Supplier is lazy — exception object created only if needed.
```

